    "complexityEstimate": "complex",
    "filteredByIgnoreCount": 25,
    "languageNotes": "Guard-dog is a Node.js CLI security scanner built with ES6 modules and native APIs. It has zero npm dependencies beyond dotenv and node-fetch. The codebase is organized into modular scanner plugins (CVE, pattern analysis, reputation, threat intelligence, VirusTotal) with a decision tree engine that assigns security verdicts (BARK, WHINE, SILENT). Extensive shell scripting handles installation, cron scheduling, git hooks, and health monitoring.",
    "languageLesson": "Key architectural pattern: multi-scanner composition with pluggable analyzers coordinated by a central decision tree. Each scanner (CVE, reputation, pattern, threat-intel, VirusTotal) operates independently and returns structured results that feed into the decision tree for deterministic verdict generation. The CLI orchestrator (src/index.js) and core engine (src/core/guard-dog.js) delegate to these scanners rather than doing analysis directly. This makes scanners independently testable and composable."
  },
